/*  Statements — ParseStatement in `src/Interpreter/Parser.cs` and the parsers it dispatches to.

    ★ The dispatch is on the FIRST token, in the C# switch's order, including the identifier cases
    that are decided by a word after it (`output`, `seed`, `make`, `current`, a pipe).
*/

Pull a book on collections.
    Bind node or failure to statement unto parser:
        Define tok as cast one's peek.
        Define kind as tok's kind.

        If kind is "State":
            Cast one's advance.
            Cast one's skip-noise.
            Define value as cast one's expression or pass the failure off.
            Cast one's skip-noise.
            Cast one's consume on ("Dot") or pass the failure off.
            Return cast made on ("StateStatement", a series with (value)).
        Done.
        If kind is "Define", return cast one's define-statement or pass the failure off.

        If kind is "Identifier":
            Define following as cast one's kind-after.
            Define lowered as tok's lexeme in lowercase.
            If lowered is "output" and following is not "Becomes" and following is not "Possessive" and following is not "Equal" and following is not "Pipe":
                Cast one's advance.
                Cast one's skip-noise.
                Define value as cast one's expression or pass the failure off.
                Return cast one's finish-with-dot on (cast placed on ("OutputStatement", a series with (value), tok)) or pass the failure off.
            Done.
            If lowered is "make" and following is "DirectoryKw":
                Cast one's advance.
                Cast one's skip-noise.
                Cast one's consume on ("DirectoryKw") or pass the failure off.
                Cast one's skip-noise.
                Define path-expr as cast one's expr-or or pass the failure off.
                Return cast one's finish-with-dot on (cast placed on ("PathActionStatement",
                    a series with (cast atom on ("MakeDirectory"), path-expr), tok)) or pass the failure off.
            Done.
            If lowered is "seed" and cast one's next-word-is on ("chance"):
                Cast one's advance.
                Cast one's skip-noise.
                If cast one's peek-kind is not "Identifier" or cast one's is-word on ("chance") is false:
                    Return a failure (cast one's expecting on (cast one's peek, "'chance' — expected after 'Seed the'")).
                Done.
                Cast one's advance.
                Cast one's skip-noise.
                Cast one's consume on ("With") or pass the failure off.
                Cast one's skip-noise.
                Define seed-value as cast one's expression or pass the failure off.
                Return cast one's finish-with-dot on (cast placed on ("SeedChanceStatement", a series with (seed-value), tok)) or pass the failure off.
            Done.
            If following is "Pipe", return cast one's pipe-statement or pass the failure off.
            If lowered is "current" and following is "DirectoryKw":
                Cast one's advance.
                Cast one's skip-noise.
                Cast one's consume on ("DirectoryKw") or pass the failure off.
                Cast one's skip-noise.
                Cast one's consume on ("Becomes") or pass the failure off.
                Cast one's skip-noise.
                Define path-expr as cast one's expression or pass the failure off.
                Return cast one's finish-with-dot on (cast placed on ("CurrentDirectorySetStatement", a series with (path-expr), tok)) or pass the failure off.
            Done.
            If cast is-ordinal-lexeme on (tok's lexeme) and following is "Of":
                Return cast one's series-set-statement or pass the failure off.
            Done.
            Return cast one's becomes-statement or pass the failure off.
        Done.

        If kind is "One":
            Cast one's advance.
            Cast one's skip-noise.
            Return cast one's possessive-set on (cast variable-named on ("one", tok)) or pass the failure off.
        Done.
        If kind is "Article", return cast one's record-named-set or pass the failure off.
        If kind is "If", return cast one's if-statement or pass the failure off.
        If kind is "While", return cast one's while-statement or pass the failure off.
        If kind is "Repeat", return cast one's repeat-until or pass the failure off.
        If kind is "Exit":
            Cast one's advance.
            Cast one's skip-noise.
            Define status as cast nothing.
            If cast one's peek-kind is "With":
                Cast one's advance.
                Cast one's skip-noise.
                The status becomes cast one's expression or pass the failure off.
                Cast one's skip-noise.
            Done.
            Cast one's consume on ("Dot") or pass the failure off.
            Return cast placed on ("ExitStatement", a series with (status), tok).
        Done.
        If kind is "Stop" or kind is "Skip":
            If one's loop-depth is 0:
                Return a failure (cast one's refused on (tok, "'{tok's lexeme}' is used outside a loop — " joined to ("it leaves the loop it is in, and there is none here" when kind is "Stop", otherwise "it moves on to the next turn of the loop it is in, and there is none here"))).
            Done.
            Cast one's advance.
            Cast one's consume on ("Dot") or pass the failure off.
            Define shape as "StopStatement" when kind is "Stop", otherwise "SkipStatement".
            Return cast made on (shape, a series of node).
        Done.
        If kind is "Item", return cast one's series-set-statement or pass the failure off.
        If kind is "Insert", return cast one's insert-statement or pass the failure off.
        If kind is "Increment" or kind is "Decrement", return cast one's increment-statement or pass the failure off.
        If kind is "Remove", return cast one's remove-statement or pass the failure off.
        If kind is "For", return cast one's for-each or pass the failure off.
        If kind is "Bind":
            Define following as cast one's kind-after.
            If following is "UnmakingKw", return cast one's unmaker-declaration or pass the failure off.
            If following is "OverloadingKw", return cast one's overload-declaration or pass the failure off.
            Return cast one's bind-statement or pass the failure off.
        Done.
        If kind is "Cast", return cast one's cast-statement or pass the failure off.
        If kind is "Return", return cast one's return-statement or pass the failure off.
        If kind is "Try", return cast one's try-statement or pass the failure off.
        If kind is "In", return cast one's map-set or pass the failure off.
        If kind is "Pull", return cast one's pull-statement or pass the failure off.
        If kind is "Run", return cast one's pipe-statement or pass the failure off.
        If kind is "Judge", return cast one's judge-statement or pass the failure off.
        If kind is "Bury":
            Return a failure (cast one's refused on (tok, "a bury needs a rabbit to do it — write 'Have <rabbit> bury <value>.' A rabbit is the "
                joined to "agent that does memory work, and burying is memory work; inside a burying function the "
                joined to "rabbit is normally a parameter: 'given (the rabbit helper, ...)'.")).
        Done.
        If kind is "Suppress":
            Cast one's advance.
            Cast one's skip-noise.
            Cast one's consume on ("Exception") or pass the failure off.
            Return cast one's finish-with-dot on (cast placed on ("SuppressStatement", a series of node, tok)) or pass the failure off.
        Done.
        If kind is "Write" or kind is "Append", return cast one's write-statement or pass the failure off.
        If kind is "With", return cast one's with-open or pass the failure off.
        If kind is "Cite":
            Cast one's advance.
            Cast one's skip-noise.
            Define name-tok as cast one's consume on ("Identifier") or pass the failure off.
            Return cast one's finish-with-dot on (cast placed on ("CiteStatement", a series with (cast quoted on (name-tok's lexeme)), tok))
                or pass the failure off.
        Done.
        If kind is "HaveKw", return cast one's have-statement or pass the failure off.
        If kind is "Send":
            Cast one's advance.
            Cast one's skip-noise.
            Define value as cast one's expression or pass the failure off.
            Cast one's skip-noise.
            Cast one's consume on ("Through") or pass the failure off.
            Cast one's skip-noise.
            Define channel as cast one's expression or pass the failure off.
            Return cast one's finish-with-dot on (cast placed on ("SendStatement", a series with (value, channel), tok)) or pass the failure off.
        Done.
        If kind is "Close":
            Cast one's advance.
            Cast one's skip-noise.
            Define channel as cast one's expression or pass the failure off.
            Return cast one's finish-with-dot on (cast placed on ("CloseStatement", a series with (channel), tok)) or pass the failure off.
        Done.
        If kind is "AcknowledgeKw":
            Cast one's advance.
            Cast one's skip-noise.
            Cast one's consume-word on ("interrupt") or pass the failure off.
            Return cast one's finish-with-dot on (cast placed on ("AcknowledgeInterruptStatement", a series of node, tok)) or pass the failure off.
        Done.
        If kind is "YieldKw":
            Cast one's advance.
            Return cast one's finish-with-dot on (cast placed on ("YieldStatement", a series of node, tok)) or pass the failure off.
        Done.
        If kind is "GetKw", return cast one's getter-declaration or pass the failure off.
        If kind is "SetKw", return cast one's setter-declaration or pass the failure off.
        Return a failure (cast one's expecting on (tok, "statement keyword")).
    Done.

    // ── Naming and changing ───────────────────────────────────────────────

    Bind node or failure to define-statement unto parser:
        Define define-tok as cast one's advance.
        Cast one's skip-noise-before-type.
        If cast one's peek-kind is "Object", return cast one's object-definition on (define-tok) or pass the failure off.
        Define shadowing as false.
        If cast one's peek-kind is "Shadow":
            Cast one's advance.
            The shadowing becomes true.
            Cast one's skip-noise.
        Done.
        Define declared as cast one's type-before-name or pass the failure off.
        Define name-tok as cast one's consume on ("Identifier") or pass the failure off.
        Cast one's skip-noise.
        // `Define c-language open-file, given (the text path), as [ … ].` — parsed for ANY Define and
        // refused by the checker for the rest; the clause sits between two commas.
        Define has-parameters as cast one's peek-kind is "Comma" and cast one's past-comma-is on ("Given").
        Define parameters as cast one's given-clause or pass the failure off.
        If has-parameters and cast one's peek-kind is "Comma":
            Cast one's advance.
            Cast one's skip-noise.
        Done.
        If cast one's peek-kind is "Equal":
            Return a failure (cast one's refused on (define-tok,
                "'=' is comparison, not assignment. A 'Define' introduces a name with 'as': "
                joined to "'Define {name-tok's lexeme} as ...'. To update a name that already exists, write "
                joined to "'{name-tok's lexeme} becomes ...'.")).
        Done.
        Cast one's consume on ("As") or pass the failure off.
        Cast one's skip-noise.
        If cast one's peek-kind is "Interface", return cast one's interface-definition on (name-tok, define-tok) or pass the failure off.
        Define value as cast nothing.
        If cast one's peek-kind is "Series":
            The value becomes cast one's series-literal or pass the failure off.
        Done.
        Otherwise:
            The value becomes cast one's expression or pass the failure off.
        Done.
        Cast one's skip-noise.
        Define permanent as false.
        If cast one's peek-kind is "Permanently":
            Cast one's advance.
            The permanent becomes true.
            Cast one's skip-noise.
        Done.
        Define released-by as cast one's free-it-with or pass the failure off.
        Cast one's consume on ("Dot") or pass the failure off.

        Define is-axiom as value's kind is "AxiomLiteral".
        If is-axiom and the number of parameters's children is greater than 0:
            Cast value's add on (cast atom on (":Parameters")).
            Cast value's add on (parameters).
        Done.
        If is-axiom and released-by's word is not "_":
            Cast value's add on (cast atom on (":ReleasedBy")).
            Cast value's add on (released-by).
        Done.

        // `Define regex <name> as [ … ]` — compiled here and lowered to an ordinary function, so
        // neither backend learns that patterns exist.
        If is-axiom and released-by's word is "_" and cast names-language on (declared, "regex"):
            If has-parameters:
                Return a failure (cast one's refused on (define-tok,
                    "a pattern cannot be 'given' anything — a value is spliced INTO a pattern, never handed to it as a parameter")).
            Done.
            // A fault is reported at the pattern itself — the `[` — as C# reports it.
            Define states as cast compiled-pattern on (value's word,
                cast numeral-value on (item 2 of value's children), cast numeral-value on (item 3 of value's children))
                or pass the failure off.
            Return cast regex-function on (name-tok's lexeme, states, define-tok).
        Done.

        If is-axiom and released-by's word is "_" and cast names-language on (declared, "cufet"):
            Define source-tok as a new token {
                the kind "Axiom", the lexeme value's word,
                the row cast numeral-value on (item 2 of value's children),
                the column cast numeral-value on (item 3 of value's children) }.
            // Says what it gives back ⇒ a function, lowered to a Bind right here.
            If declared's kind is "AxiomType" and (item 2 of declared's children)'s word is not "_":
                Define held-body as cast one's held-cufet on (source-tok, true) or pass the failure off.
                Define lowered as cast made on ("BindStatement", a series with (cast quoted on (name-tok's lexeme),
                    item 2 of declared's children, parameters, held-body, cast nothing, cast nothing,
                    cast row-of on (define-tok), cast column-of on (define-tok))).
                Cast lowered's add on (cast atom on (":FromAxiomLanguage")).
                Cast lowered's add on (cast quoted on ("cufet")).
                Return lowered.
            Done.
            Define held-source as cast one's held-cufet on (source-tok, false) or pass the failure off.
            Define holding as cast placed on ("CufetAxiomDefinition", a series with (cast quoted on (name-tok's lexeme), held-source), define-tok).
            If has-parameters:
                Cast holding's add on (cast atom on (":HasParameterClause")).
                Cast holding's add on (cast flag on (true)).
            Done.
            Return holding.
        Done.

        Define defined as cast made on ("DefineStatement", a series with (cast quoted on (name-tok's lexeme), value,
            cast flag on (permanent), cast flag on (shadowing),
            cast row-of on (define-tok), cast column-of on (define-tok), declared)).
        If has-parameters:
            Cast defined's add on (cast atom on (":HasParameterClause")).
            Cast defined's add on (cast flag on (true)).
        Done.
        Return defined.
    Done.

    Bind fact to is-module-conformer, given (the node conformed):
        For each claimed in conformed's children, repeat:
            Define lowered as claimed's word in lowercase.
            If lowered is "\"module\"" or lowered is "\"book\"" or lowered is "\"region\"", return true.
        Done.
        Return false.
    Done.

    /// `Define object <name> [of <blank>…] [with (…)] [and as a <type>] [and <interface>…][: … Done.]`
    Bind node or failure to object-definition unto parser, given (the token define-tok):
        Cast one's consume on ("Object") or pass the failure off.
        Cast one's skip-noise.
        Define name-tok as cast one's consume on ("Identifier") or pass the failure off.
        Cast one's skip-noise.
        Define blanks as cast listed.
        While cast one's peek-kind is "Of", repeat:
            Cast one's advance.
            Cast one's skip-noise.
            Define blank-tok as cast one's consume on ("Identifier") or pass the failure off.
            Cast blanks's add on (cast quoted on (blank-tok's lexeme)).
            Cast one's skip-noise.
        Done.
        Define permanent as cast listed.
        Define defaults as cast listed.
        Define shape as cast made on ("RecordType", a series with (cast listed, cast listed)).
        If cast one's peek-kind is "With":
            Cast one's advance.
            Cast one's skip-noise.
            The shape becomes cast one's shape-into on (permanent, defaults) or pass the failure off.
        Done.
        Cast one's skip-noise.
        Define embedded as cast nothing.
        Define conformed as cast listed.
        While cast one's peek-kind is "And", repeat:
            Cast one's advance.
            Cast one's skip-noise.
            If cast one's peek-kind is "As":
                Cast one's advance.
                Cast one's skip-noise.
                Define embedded-tok as cast one's consume on ("Identifier") or pass the failure off.
                The embedded becomes cast quoted on (embedded-tok's lexeme).
            Done.
            Otherwise:
                Define claimed-tok as cast one's consume on ("Identifier") or pass the failure off.
                Cast conformed's add on (cast quoted on (claimed-tok's lexeme)).
            Done.
            Cast one's skip-noise.
        Done.
        Define methods as cast listed.
        Define getters as cast listed.
        Define setters as cast listed.
        Define carried as cast listed.
        Define is-module as cast is-module-conformer on (conformed).
        If cast one's peek-kind is "Colon":
            Cast one's advance.
            One's in-object-def becomes true.
            Increment one's nest-depth by 1.
            Define scanning as true.
            While scanning, repeat:
                Cast one's skip-noise.
                Define kind as cast one's peek-kind.
                If kind is "Done" or kind is "Eof", stop.
                If kind is "Bind":
                    Define method as cast one's bind-statement or pass the failure off.
                    Cast methods's add on (method).
                Done.
                Otherwise if kind is "GetKw":
                    Define getter as cast one's getter-declaration or pass the failure off.
                    Cast getters's add on (getter).
                Done.
                Otherwise if kind is "SetKw":
                    Define setter as cast one's setter-declaration or pass the failure off.
                    Cast setters's add on (setter).
                Done.
                Otherwise if kind is "Define" and is-module:
                    Define was-in-object as one's in-object-def.
                    Define carried-tok as cast one's advance.
                    Cast one's skip-noise-before-type.
                    Define inner as cast one's object-definition on (carried-tok) or pass the failure off.
                    Cast carried's add on (inner).
                    One's in-object-def becomes was-in-object.
                Done.
                Otherwise if kind is "Define":
                    Return a failure (cast one's expecting on (cast one's peek,
                        "Bind, Get, or Set — only a module may declare a type inside its body, and "
                        joined to "'{name-tok's lexeme}' is not one. Add 'and module' to its declaration, or move the type "
                        joined to "outside this body")).
                Done.
                Otherwise:
                    Return a failure (cast one's expecting on (cast one's peek,
                        "Bind, Get, or Set — only method, getter, and setter definitions are allowed inside an object body")).
                Done.
            Done.
            Decrement one's nest-depth by 1.
            One's in-object-def becomes false.
            Cast one's consume on ("Done") or pass the failure off.
            Cast one's consume on ("Dot") or pass the failure off.
        Done.
        Otherwise:
            Cast one's consume on ("Dot") or pass the failure off.
        Done.
        Return cast made on ("ObjectDefinition", a series with (cast quoted on (name-tok's lexeme),
            item 1 of shape's children, item 2 of shape's children, methods, getters, setters, embedded,
            conformed, cast row-of on (define-tok), cast column-of on (define-tok), permanent, blanks,
            carried, defaults)).
    Done.

    /// A compiled pattern as the function the C# parser lowers it to: `given (the text subject)`,
    /// and one `Return` that runs the engine over the states and the subject.
    Bind node to regex-function, given (the text name,
            the series of records like (the number kind, the text ch, the number step, the number alt) states,
            the token define-tok):
        Define elements as cast listed.
        For each one-state in states, repeat:
            Define fields as cast listed.
            For each field-name in a series with ("kind", "ch", "step", "alt"), repeat:
                Define field-pair as cast listed.
                Cast field-pair's add on (cast quoted on (field-name)).
                If field-name is "kind", cast field-pair's add on (cast made on ("NumberLiteral", a series with (cast numeral on (the kind of one-state)))).
                If field-name is "ch", cast field-pair's add on (cast made on ("StringLiteral", a series with (cast quoted on (the ch of one-state)))).
                If field-name is "step", cast field-pair's add on (cast made on ("NumberLiteral", a series with (cast numeral on (the step of one-state)))).
                If field-name is "alt", cast field-pair's add on (cast made on ("NumberLiteral", a series with (cast numeral on (the alt of one-state)))).
                Cast fields's add on (field-pair).
            Done.
            Cast elements's add on (cast placed on ("RecordLiteral", a series with (cast listed, fields), define-tok)).
        Done.
        Define state-fields as cast listed.
        For each shape-field in a series with ("alt", "ch", "kind", "step"), repeat:
            Define shape-pair as cast listed.
            Cast shape-pair's add on (cast quoted on (shape-field)).
            If shape-field is "ch":
                Cast shape-pair's add on (cast plain-type on ("TextType")).
            Done.
            Otherwise:
                Cast shape-pair's add on (cast plain-type on ("NumberType")).
            Done.
            Cast state-fields's add on (shape-pair).
        Done.
        Define state-type as cast made on ("RecordType", a series with (cast listed, state-fields)).
        Define automaton as cast placed on ("SeriesLiteral", a series with (elements, state-type), define-tok).
        Define call-args as cast listed.
        Cast call-args's add on (automaton).
        Cast call-args's add on (cast variable-named on ("subject", define-tok)).
        Define engine-call as cast placed on ("CastExpression", a series with (
            cast variable-named on ("match in regex", define-tok), call-args), define-tok).
        Define body as cast listed.
        Cast body's add on (cast placed on ("ReturnStatement", a series with (engine-call), define-tok)).
        Define subject-pair as cast listed.
        Cast subject-pair's add on (cast plain-type on ("TextType")).
        Cast subject-pair's add on (cast quoted on ("subject")).
        Define taking as cast listed.
        Cast taking's add on (subject-pair).
        Define lowered as cast made on ("BindStatement", a series with (cast quoted on (name), cast plain-type on ("FactType"),
            taking, body, cast nothing, cast nothing, cast row-of on (define-tok), cast column-of on (define-tok))).
        Cast lowered's add on (cast atom on (":FromAxiomLanguage")).
        Cast lowered's add on (cast quoted on ("regex")).
        Return lowered.
    Done.

    /// `, and free it with <name>` — the release half of an acquiring axiom. Nothing when absent.
    Bind node or failure to free-it-with unto parser:
        If cast one's peek-kind is not "Comma", return cast nothing.
        Define second-tok as cast one's token-at on (one's at + 1).
        Define third-tok as cast one's token-at on (one's at + 2).
        If second-tok's kind is not "And", return cast nothing.
        If third-tok's kind is not "Identifier" or cast spelled on (third-tok, "free") is false, return cast nothing.
        Cast one's advance.
        Cast one's skip-noise.
        Cast one's advance.
        Cast one's skip-noise.
        Cast one's advance.
        Cast one's skip-noise.
        Cast one's consume on ("It") or pass the failure off.
        Cast one's skip-noise.
        Cast one's consume on ("With") or pass the failure off.
        Cast one's skip-noise.
        Define name-tok as cast one's consume on ("Identifier") or pass the failure off.
        Cast one's skip-noise.
        Return cast quoted on (name-tok's lexeme).
    Done.

    /// NamesRegex / NamesCufet — the declared type names that language's tag.
    Bind fact to names-language, given (the node declared, the text language):
        Define wanted as "\"" joined to language joined to "\"".
        If declared's kind is "ObjectType" or declared's kind is "AxiomType":
            Return ((item 1 of declared's children)'s word in lowercase) is wanted.
        Done.
        Return false.
    Done.

    Bind number to numeral-value, given (the node leaf):
        Return (leaf's word converted to number) but void is 0.
    Done.

    Bind node or failure to becomes-statement unto parser:
        Define name-tok as cast one's consume on ("Identifier") or pass the failure off.
        Cast one's skip-noise.
        If cast one's peek-kind is "Possessive":
            Return cast one's possessive-set on (cast variable-named on (name-tok's lexeme, name-tok)) or pass the failure off.
        Done.
        If cast one's peek-kind is "Equal":
            Return a failure (cast one's refused on (name-tok,
                "'=' is comparison, not assignment. Did you mean '{name-tok's lexeme} becomes ...' (update) "
                joined to "or 'Define {name-tok's lexeme} as ...' (introduce)?")).
        Done.
        Cast one's consume on ("Becomes") or pass the failure off.
        Cast one's skip-noise.
        Define value as cast one's expression or pass the failure off.
        Cast one's skip-noise.
        Cast one's consume on ("Dot") or pass the failure off.
        Return cast placed on ("BecomesStatement", a series with (cast quoted on (name-tok's lexeme), value), name-tok).
    Done.

    Bind node or failure to possessive-set unto parser, given (the node target):
        Define owns as cast one's consume on ("Possessive") or pass the failure off.
        Cast one's skip-noise.
        Define member as cast one's advance.
        Cast one's skip-noise.
        Cast one's consume on ("Becomes") or pass the failure off.
        Cast one's skip-noise.
        Define value as cast one's expression or pass the failure off.
        Cast one's skip-noise.
        Cast one's consume on ("Dot") or pass the failure off.
        Return cast placed on ("PossessiveSetStatement", a series with (target, cast quoted on (member's lexeme), value), owns).
    Done.

    Bind node or failure to record-named-set unto parser:
        Cast one's consume on ("Article") or pass the failure off.
        Define field-tok as cast one's advance.
        Cast one's skip-noise.
        Cast one's consume on ("Of") or pass the failure off.
        Cast one's skip-noise.
        Define whole as cast one's postfix or pass the failure off.
        Cast one's skip-noise.
        Cast one's consume on ("Becomes") or pass the failure off.
        Cast one's skip-noise.
        Define value as cast one's expression or pass the failure off.
        Cast one's skip-noise.
        Cast one's consume on ("Dot") or pass the failure off.
        Return cast placed on ("RecordNamedSetStatement", a series with (cast quoted on (field-tok's lexeme), whole, value), field-tok).
    Done.

    /// `The item 3 of s becomes 1.` / `The first of s becomes 1.`
    Bind node or failure to series-set-statement unto parser:
        If cast one's peek-kind is "Item" and cast one's next-word-is on ("at") and cast one's kind-two-after is "LParen":
            Define item-tok as cast one's advance.
            Cast one's skip-noise.
            Cast one's advance.
            Cast one's skip-noise.
            Cast one's consume on ("LParen") or pass the failure off.
            Cast one's skip-noise.
            Define row as cast one's expression or pass the failure off.
            Cast one's skip-noise.
            Cast one's consume on ("Comma") or pass the failure off.
            Cast one's skip-noise.
            Define column as cast one's expression or pass the failure off.
            Cast one's skip-noise.
            Cast one's consume on ("RParen") or pass the failure off.
            Cast one's skip-noise.
            Cast one's consume on ("Of") or pass the failure off.
            Cast one's skip-noise.
            Define grid as cast one's core-primary or pass the failure off.
            Cast one's skip-noise.
            Cast one's consume on ("Becomes") or pass the failure off.
            Cast one's skip-noise.
            Define value as cast one's expression or pass the failure off.
            Return cast one's finish-with-dot on (cast placed on ("MatrixSetStatement", a series with (grid, row, column, value), item-tok))
                or pass the failure off.
        Done.
        Define lead as cast one's peek.
        Define index as cast nothing.
        If lead's kind is "Identifier" and cast is-ordinal-lexeme on (lead's lexeme):
            Cast one's advance.
            The index becomes cast ordinal-index on (lead's lexeme).
        Done.
        Otherwise:
            Cast one's consume on ("Item") or pass the failure off.
            Cast one's skip-noise.
            The index becomes cast one's expression or pass the failure off.
        Done.
        Cast one's skip-noise.
        Cast one's consume on ("Of") or pass the failure off.
        Cast one's skip-noise.
        Define whole as cast one's core-primary or pass the failure off.
        Cast one's skip-noise.
        Cast one's consume on ("Becomes") or pass the failure off.
        Cast one's skip-noise.
        Define value as cast one's expression or pass the failure off.
        Cast one's skip-noise.
        Cast one's consume on ("Dot") or pass the failure off.
        Return cast placed on ("SeriesSetStatement", a series with (whole, index, value), lead).
    Done.

    /// `Increment <target> by <amount>.` — sugar, desugared here into the `becomes` it stands for.
    Bind node or failure to increment-statement unto parser:
        Define verb as cast one's advance.
        Define op as "Plus" when verb's kind is "Increment", otherwise "Minus".
        Cast one's skip-noise.
        Define name-tok as cast one's peek.
        If name-tok's kind is "One":
            Cast one's advance.
        Done.
        Otherwise:
            The name-tok becomes cast one's consume on ("Identifier") or pass the failure off.
        Done.
        Define name as "one" when name-tok's kind is "One", otherwise name-tok's lexeme.
        Define target as cast variable-named on (name, name-tok).
        Cast one's skip-noise.
        Define member as "".
        Define owns as name-tok.
        If cast one's peek-kind is "Possessive":
            The owns becomes cast one's advance.
            Cast one's skip-noise.
            Define member-tok as cast one's advance.
            The member becomes member-tok's lexeme.
            Cast one's skip-noise.
        Done.
        Cast one's consume on ("By") or pass the failure off.
        Cast one's skip-noise.
        Define amount as cast one's expression or pass the failure off.
        Cast one's skip-noise.
        Cast one's consume on ("Dot") or pass the failure off.
        If member is "":
            Return cast placed on ("BecomesStatement", a series with (cast quoted on (name),
                cast binary on (target, op, amount, name-tok)), name-tok).
        Done.
        Define read as cast placed on ("PossessiveAccess", a series with (target, cast quoted on (member)), owns).
        Return cast placed on ("PossessiveSetStatement", a series with (target, cast quoted on (member),
            cast binary on (read, op, amount, owns)), owns).
    Done.

    // ── Collections ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    Bind node or failure to insert-statement unto parser:
        Define insert-tok as cast one's advance.
        Cast one's skip-noise.
        Define value as cast one's expression or pass the failure off.
        Cast one's skip-noise.
        Define after-spot as cast nothing.
        Define to-start as false.
        If cast one's peek-kind is "Into":
            Cast one's advance.
            Cast one's skip-noise.
            If cast one's peek-kind is "Start":
                Cast one's advance.
                Cast one's skip-noise.
                Cast one's consume on ("Of") or pass the failure off.
                Cast one's skip-noise.
                The to-start becomes true.
            Done.
        Done.
        Otherwise:
            Cast one's consume on ("After") or pass the failure off.
            Cast one's skip-noise.
            Define lead as cast one's peek.
            If lead's kind is "Identifier" and cast is-ordinal-lexeme on (lead's lexeme):
                Cast one's advance.
                The after-spot becomes cast ordinal-index on (lead's lexeme).
                Cast one's skip-noise.
                If cast one's peek-kind is "Item", cast one's advance.
            Done.
            Otherwise:
                Cast one's consume on ("Item") or pass the failure off.
                Cast one's skip-noise.
                The after-spot becomes cast one's expression or pass the failure off.
            Done.
            Cast one's skip-noise.
            Cast one's consume on ("Of") or pass the failure off.
            Cast one's skip-noise.
        Done.
        Define whole as cast one's core-primary or pass the failure off.
        Cast one's skip-noise.
        Cast one's consume on ("Dot") or pass the failure off.
        Return cast placed on ("SeriesInsertStatement", a series with (value, whole, after-spot, cast flag on (to-start)), insert-tok).
    Done.

    Bind node or failure to remove-statement unto parser:
        Define remove-tok as cast one's advance.
        Cast one's skip-noise.
        If cast one's peek-kind is "File" or cast one's peek-kind is "DirectoryKw":
            Define what as cast one's advance.
            Define action as "RemoveFile" when what's kind is "File", otherwise "RemoveDirectory".
            Cast one's skip-noise.
            Define path-expr as cast one's expr-or or pass the failure off.
            Return cast one's finish-with-dot on (cast placed on ("PathActionStatement",
                a series with (cast atom on (action), path-expr), remove-tok)) or pass the failure off.
        Done.
        Define lead as cast one's peek.
        If lead's kind is "Identifier" and cast is-ordinal-lexeme on (lead's lexeme):
            Cast one's advance.
            Define index as cast ordinal-index on (lead's lexeme).
            Cast one's skip-noise.
            If cast one's peek-kind is "Item", cast one's advance.
            Cast one's skip-noise.
            Cast one's consume on ("From") or pass the failure off.
            Cast one's skip-noise.
            Define whole as cast one's core-primary or pass the failure off.
            Cast one's skip-noise.
            Cast one's consume on ("Dot") or pass the failure off.
            Return cast placed on ("SeriesRemoveAtStatement", a series with (whole, index), remove-tok).
        Done.
        If lead's kind is "Item":
            Cast one's advance.
            Cast one's skip-noise.
            Define index as cast one's expression or pass the failure off.
            Cast one's skip-noise.
            Cast one's consume on ("From") or pass the failure off.
            Cast one's skip-noise.
            Define whole as cast one's core-primary or pass the failure off.
            Cast one's skip-noise.
            Cast one's consume on ("Dot") or pass the failure off.
            Return cast placed on ("SeriesRemoveAtStatement", a series with (whole, index), remove-tok).
        Done.
        Define value as cast one's expression or pass the failure off.
        Cast one's skip-noise.
        Cast one's consume on ("From") or pass the failure off.
        Cast one's skip-noise.
        Define whole as cast one's core-primary or pass the failure off.
        Cast one's skip-noise.
        Cast one's consume on ("Dot") or pass the failure off.
        Return cast placed on ("SeriesRemoveValueStatement", a series with (whole, value), remove-tok).
    Done.

    Bind node or failure to map-set unto parser:
        Define in-tok as cast one's advance.
        Cast one's skip-noise.
        Define whole as cast one's postfix or pass the failure off.
        Cast one's skip-noise.
        Cast one's consume on ("Comma") or pass the failure off.
        Cast one's skip-noise.
        Cast one's consume-word on ("entry") or pass the failure off.
        Cast one's skip-noise.
        Cast one's consume on ("For") or pass the failure off.
        Cast one's skip-noise.
        Define key as cast one's expression or pass the failure off.
        Cast one's skip-noise.
        Cast one's consume on ("Becomes") or pass the failure off.
        Cast one's skip-noise.
        Define value as cast one's expression or pass the failure off.
        Cast one's skip-noise.
        Cast one's consume on ("Dot") or pass the failure off.
        Return cast placed on ("MapSetStatement", a series with (whole, key, value), in-tok).
    Done.

    // ── Choosing and repeating ────────────────────────────────────────────

    Bind node or failure to if-statement unto parser:
        Define arms as cast listed.
        Define otherwise-body as cast nothing.
        Define if-tok as cast one's consume on ("If") or pass the failure off.
        Cast one's skip-noise.
        Define first-condition as cast one's condition or pass the failure off.
        Define first-body as cast one's if-body on (if-tok) or pass the failure off.
        Cast arms's add on (cast made on ("ConditionArm", a series with (first-condition, first-body))).
        Define scanning as true.
        While scanning, repeat:
            Cast one's skip-noise.
            If cast one's peek-kind is not "Otherwise", stop.
            Define otherwise-tok as cast one's advance.
            Cast one's skip-noise.
            If cast one's peek-kind is "If":
                Define else-if-tok as cast one's advance.
                Cast one's skip-noise.
                Define condition as cast one's condition or pass the failure off.
                Define body as cast one's if-body on (else-if-tok) or pass the failure off.
                Cast arms's add on (cast made on ("ConditionArm", a series with (condition, body))).
            Done.
            Otherwise:
                The otherwise-body becomes cast one's if-body on (otherwise-tok) or pass the failure off.
                The scanning becomes false.
            Done.
        Done.
        Return cast made on ("IfStatement", a series with (arms, otherwise-body)).
    Done.

    /// A comma and ONE statement, or a colon and a block closed by `Done.`
    Bind node or failure to if-body unto parser, given (the token opener):
        Cast one's skip-noise.
        If cast one's peek-kind is "Comma":
            Cast one's advance.
            Cast one's skip-noise.
            Increment one's nest-depth by 1.
            Define single as cast one's statement or pass the failure off.
            Decrement one's nest-depth by 1.
            Define body as cast listed.
            Cast body's add on (single).
            Return body.
        Done.
        Cast one's consume on ("Colon") or pass the failure off.
        Increment one's nest-depth by 1.
        Define body as cast one's loop-body on (opener, "If x is 1, state \"one\".", "", "Otherwise") or pass the failure off.
        Decrement one's nest-depth by 1.
        Return body.
    Done.

    /// Unclosed — a block the file ended inside, named at the word that opened it.
    Bind text to unclosed, given (the token opener, the text example, the text construct):
        Define called as opener's lexeme.
        If construct is not "", the called becomes construct.
        Define advice as "Close it with 'Done.'.".
        If example is not "":
            The advice becomes "Either close it with 'Done.', or — if the body is a single statement — write the "
                joined to "inline form instead, which takes a comma and no 'Done.': '{example}'".
        Done.
        Return cast refused-at on (opener's row, opener's column,
            "this '{called}' opens a block, and the file ended before its 'Done.'. " joined to advice).
    Done.

    /// UnclosedBeforeArm — a block left open by the next arm arriving.
    Bind text to unclosed-before-arm, given (the token opener, the token found, the text construct):
        Define called as opener's lexeme.
        If construct is not "", the called becomes construct.
        Return cast refused-at on (opener's row, opener's column,
            "this '{called}' opens a block, and '{found's lexeme}' arrived on "
            joined to "line {found's row} before its 'Done.'. In the block form every arm closes before the "
            joined to "next one begins: 'If x is 1: ... Done. Otherwise: ... Done.'. The INLINE form is the "
            joined to "one that needs no 'Done.': 'If x is 1, state \"one\". Otherwise, state \"other\".'").
    Done.

    /// ParseLoopBody — statements up to `Done.`, at least one. A `continuation` (an `Otherwise`)
    /// arriving first means the block was never closed.
    Bind node or failure to loop-body unto parser, given (the token opener, the text example,
            the text construct, the text continuation):
        Define body as cast listed.
        Define scanning as true.
        While scanning, repeat:
            Cast one's skip-noise.
            Define kind as cast one's peek-kind.
            If kind is "Done" or kind is "Eof", stop.
            If continuation is not "" and kind is continuation:
                Return a failure (cast unclosed-before-arm on (opener, cast one's peek, construct)).
            Done.
            Define inner as cast one's statement or pass the failure off.
            Cast body's add on (inner).
        Done.
        If the number of body's children is 0:
            Return a failure (cast one's expecting on (cast one's peek, "at least one statement in loop body")).
        Done.
        If cast one's peek-kind is "Eof":
            Return a failure (cast unclosed on (opener, example, construct)).
        Done.
        Cast one's consume on ("Done") or pass the failure off.
        Cast one's consume on ("Dot") or pass the failure off.
        Return body.
    Done.

    /// A loop's body: `repeat:` and a block, or one statement.
    Bind node or failure to loop-body-or-inline unto parser:
        Cast one's skip-noise.
        Increment one's loop-depth by 1.
        Increment one's nest-depth by 1.
        Define body as cast listed.
        If cast one's peek-kind is "Repeat":
            Define repeat-tok as cast one's advance.
            Cast one's skip-noise.
            Cast one's consume on ("Colon") or pass the failure off.
            The body becomes cast one's loop-body on (repeat-tok, "For each n in items, State n.", "", "") or pass the failure off.
        Done.
        Otherwise:
            Define single as cast one's statement or pass the failure off.
            Cast body's add on (single).
        Done.
        Decrement one's nest-depth by 1.
        Decrement one's loop-depth by 1.
        Return body.
    Done.

    Bind node or failure to while-statement unto parser:
        Cast one's advance.
        Cast one's skip-noise.
        Define condition as cast one's condition or pass the failure off.
        Cast one's skip-noise.
        Cast one's consume on ("Comma") or pass the failure off.
        Define body as cast one's loop-body-or-inline or pass the failure off.
        Return cast made on ("WhileStatement", a series with (condition, body)).
    Done.

    Bind node or failure to repeat-until unto parser:
        Cast one's advance.
        Cast one's skip-noise.
        Cast one's consume on ("Colon") or pass the failure off.
        Increment one's loop-depth by 1.
        Increment one's nest-depth by 1.
        Define body as cast listed.
        Define scanning as true.
        While scanning, repeat:
            Cast one's skip-noise.
            If cast one's peek-kind is "Until" or cast one's peek-kind is "Eof", stop.
            Define inner as cast one's statement or pass the failure off.
            Cast body's add on (inner).
        Done.
        If the number of body's children is 0:
            Return a failure (cast one's expecting on (cast one's peek, "at least one statement in repeat-until body")).
        Done.
        Decrement one's nest-depth by 1.
        Decrement one's loop-depth by 1.
        Cast one's consume on ("Until") or pass the failure off.
        Cast one's skip-noise.
        Define condition as cast one's condition or pass the failure off.
        Cast one's skip-noise.
        Cast one's consume on ("Dot") or pass the failure off.
        Return cast made on ("RepeatUntilStatement", a series with (body, condition)).
    Done.

    Bind node or failure to for-each unto parser:
        Define for-tok as cast one's advance.
        Cast one's skip-noise.
        Cast one's consume on ("Each") or pass the failure off.
        Cast one's skip-noise.
        Define iterator as cast nothing.
        If cast one's peek-kind is "Identifier" or cast one's peek-kind is "Item":
            Define name-tok as cast one's advance.
            The iterator becomes cast quoted on (name-tok's lexeme).
            Cast one's skip-noise.
        Done.
        // A word-shaped token still here is RESERVED — the slot above takes every identifier.
        Otherwise if cast one's looks-like-a-word on (cast one's peek) and cast one's peek-kind is not "In" and cast one's peek-kind is not "From":
            Return a failure (cast one's reserved-as-name on (cast one's peek)).
        Done.
        If cast one's peek-kind is "From":
            Cast one's advance.
            Cast one's skip-noise.
            If cast one's peek-kind is not "Identifier" or cast one's is-word on ("input") is false:
                Return a failure (cast one's expecting on (cast one's peek, "'input' (in 'for each ... from the input:')")).
            Done.
            Cast one's advance.
            Cast one's skip-noise.
            Increment one's loop-depth by 1.
            Increment one's nest-depth by 1.
            Define consumer-body as cast listed.
            If cast one's peek-kind is "Comma":
                Cast one's advance.
                Cast one's skip-noise.
                Define single as cast one's statement or pass the failure off.
                Cast consumer-body's add on (single).
            Done.
            Otherwise:
                Define colon-tok as cast one's consume on ("Colon") or pass the failure off.
                The consumer-body becomes cast one's loop-body on (colon-tok, "For each n in items, State n.", "", "") or pass the failure off.
            Done.
            Decrement one's nest-depth by 1.
            Decrement one's loop-depth by 1.
            Define consumer-name as "it".
            If iterator's word is not "_":
                Define name-length as the length of iterator's word.
                The consumer-name becomes the characters from 2 to (name-length - 1) of iterator's word.
            Done.
            Return cast placed on ("ForEachFromInputStatement", a series with (cast quoted on (consumer-name), consumer-body), for-tok).
        Done.
        Cast one's consume on ("In") or pass the failure off.
        Cast one's skip-noise.
        Define over as cast one's expression or pass the failure off.
        Cast one's skip-noise.
        Cast one's consume on ("Comma") or pass the failure off.
        Define body as cast one's loop-body-or-inline or pass the failure off.
        Return cast placed on ("ForEachStatement", a series with (iterator, over, body), for-tok).
    Done.

    // ── Conditions ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    Bind node or failure to condition unto parser:
        Define left as cast one's logical-xor or pass the failure off.
        While cast one's peek-kind is "Or", repeat:
            Define op-tok as cast one's advance.
            Cast one's skip-noise.
            Define right as cast one's logical-xor or pass the failure off.
            The left becomes cast binary on (left, "Or", right, op-tok).
        Done.
        Return left.
    Done.

    Bind node or failure to logical-xor unto parser:
        Define left as cast one's logical-and or pass the failure off.
        While cast one's peek-kind is "Xor", repeat:
            Define op-tok as cast one's advance.
            Cast one's skip-noise.
            Define right as cast one's logical-and or pass the failure off.
            The left becomes cast binary on (left, "Xor", right, op-tok).
        Done.
        Return left.
    Done.

    Bind node or failure to logical-and unto parser:
        Define left as cast one's cond-not or pass the failure off.
        While cast one's peek-kind is "And", repeat:
            Define op-tok as cast one's advance.
            Cast one's skip-noise.
            Define right as cast one's cond-not or pass the failure off.
            The left becomes cast binary on (left, "And", right, op-tok).
        Done.
        Return left.
    Done.

    Bind node or failure to cond-not unto parser:
        If cast one's peek-kind is "Not":
            Define not-tok as cast one's advance.
            Cast one's skip-noise.
            Define operand as cast one's cond-not or pass the failure off.
            Return cast unary on ("Not", operand, not-tok).
        Done.
        Return cast one's single-condition or pass the failure off.
    Done.

    Bind node or failure to single-condition unto parser:
        Cast one's skip-noise.
        Define left as cast one's joined-to or pass the failure off.
        Cast one's skip-noise.
        If cast is-symbol-comparison on (cast one's peek-kind):
            Define op-tok as cast one's advance.
            Cast one's skip-noise.
            Define right as cast one's joined-to or pass the failure off.
            Return cast binary on (left, op-tok's kind, right, op-tok).
        Done.
        If cast one's peek-kind is not "Is", return left.
        Define is-tok as cast one's advance.
        Return cast one's after-is on (left, is-tok) or pass the failure off.
    Done.

    // ── Functions ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    Bind node or failure to cast-statement unto parser:
        Define call as cast one's cast-expression or pass the failure off.
        Cast one's skip-noise.
        Define passes-off as false.
        If cast one's peek-kind is "Or" and cast one's kind-after is "Pass":
            Cast one's advance.
            Cast one's skip-noise.
            Cast one's consume on ("Pass") or pass the failure off.
            Cast one's skip-noise.
            Cast one's consume on ("Failure") or pass the failure off.
            Cast one's skip-noise.
            Cast one's consume on ("Off") or pass the failure off.
            Cast one's skip-noise.
            The passes-off becomes true.
        Done.
        Cast one's consume on ("Dot") or pass the failure off.
        // A statement carries the call's own fields, in the same order, then what the parser set on it.
        Define statement as cast made on ("CastStatement", call's children).
        If passes-off:
            Cast statement's add on (cast atom on (":PassesFailureOff")).
            Cast statement's add on (cast flag on (true)).
        Done.
        Return statement.
    Done.

    Bind node or failure to return-statement unto parser:
        Define return-tok as cast one's advance.
        If one's function-depth is 0:
            Return a failure (cast one's refused on (return-tok, "'Return' is used outside a function — it gives a function's answer back, and there is no function here")).
        Done.
        Cast one's skip-noise.
        If cast one's peek-kind is "Dot":
            Cast one's advance.
            Return cast placed on ("ReturnStatement", a series with (cast nothing), return-tok).
        Done.
        Define value as cast one's expression or pass the failure off.
        Cast one's skip-noise.
        Cast one's consume on ("Dot") or pass the failure off.
        Return cast placed on ("ReturnStatement", a series with (value), return-tok).
    Done.

    Bind node or failure to bind-statement unto parser:
        Define bind-tok as cast one's advance.
        If one's nest-depth is greater than 0 and one's in-object-def is false and one's in-free-function is false:
            Return a failure (cast one's refused on (bind-tok,
                "functions can only be declared at the top level or inside another function, not inside a block")).
        Done.
        Define saved-object-def as one's in-object-def.
        Define saved-free-function as one's in-free-function.
        One's in-object-def becomes false.
        Cast one's skip-noise.
        Define constructs as cast nothing.
        Define returned as cast nothing.
        If cast one's peek-kind is "MakingKw":
            Cast one's advance.
            Cast one's skip-noise.
            Define made-tok as cast one's consume on ("Identifier") or pass the failure off.
            Cast one's skip-noise.
            The constructs becomes cast quoted on (made-tok's lexeme).
            The returned becomes cast made on ("ObjectType", a series with (cast quoted on (made-tok's lexeme), cast listed)).
            If cast one's peek-kind is "Or" and cast one's kind-after is "Failure":
                Cast one's advance.
                Cast one's skip-noise.
                Cast one's consume on ("Failure") or pass the failure off.
                Cast one's skip-noise.
                The returned becomes cast made on ("FailureType", a series with (returned)).
            Done.
        Done.
        Otherwise:
            The returned becomes cast one's return-type or pass the failure off.
            Cast one's skip-noise.
        Done.
        Cast one's consume on ("To") or pass the failure off.
        Cast one's skip-noise.
        Define name-tok as cast one's consume on ("Identifier") or pass the failure off.
        Cast one's skip-noise.
        Define unto-name as cast nothing.
        If cast one's peek-kind is "Unto":
            Cast one's advance.
            Cast one's skip-noise.
            The unto-name becomes cast one's unto-target or pass the failure off.
            Cast one's skip-noise.
        Done.
        Define parameters as cast one's given-clause or pass the failure off.
        Define when-clause as cast nothing.
        Cast one's skip-noise.
        If cast one's peek-kind is "When":
            Cast one's advance.
            Cast one's skip-noise.
            The when-clause becomes cast one's expression or pass the failure off.
            Cast one's skip-noise.
        Done.
        One's in-free-function becomes unto-name's word is "_" and constructs's word is "_" and saved-object-def is false.
        Increment one's function-depth by 1.
        Define body as cast listed.
        If returned's word is "_" or cast is-void-or-failure on (returned):
            The body becomes cast one's void-body on (bind-tok, "Bind void to greet, State \"hi\".", "") or pass the failure off.
        Done.
        Otherwise:
            The body becomes cast one's value-body on (bind-tok, "Bind number to double, given (the number n), n * 2.", "") or pass the failure off.
        Done.
        Decrement one's function-depth by 1.
        One's in-object-def becomes saved-object-def.
        One's in-free-function becomes saved-free-function.
        Define bound as cast made on ("BindStatement", a series with (cast quoted on (name-tok's lexeme), returned,
            parameters, body, unto-name, constructs, cast row-of on (bind-tok), cast column-of on (bind-tok))).
        If when-clause's word is not "_":
            Cast bound's add on (cast atom on (":When")).
            Cast bound's add on (when-clause).
        Done.
        Return bound.
    Done.

    /// ParseReturnType — nothing for a bare `void`.
    Bind node or failure to return-type unto parser:
        Increment one's type-depth by 1.
        Define parsed as cast one's return-type-core or pass the failure off.
        Decrement one's type-depth by 1.
        Return parsed.
    Done.

    Bind node or failure to return-type-core unto parser:
        If cast one's peek-kind is "Void":
            Cast one's advance.
            Cast one's skip-noise.
            If cast one's peek-kind is "Or" and cast one's kind-after is "Failure":
                Cast one's advance.
                Cast one's skip-noise.
                Cast one's consume on ("Failure") or pass the failure off.
                Cast one's skip-noise.
                Return cast made on ("FailureType", a series with (cast plain-type on ("VoidType"))).
            Done.
            If cast one's peek-kind is not "FunctionKw", return cast nothing.
            Cast one's advance.
            Cast one's skip-noise.
            Define parameters as cast one's function-param-type-list or pass the failure off.
            Return cast made on ("FunctionType", a series with (parameters, cast nothing)).
        Done.
        If cast one's peek-kind is "Record":
            Cast one's advance.
            Cast one's skip-noise.
            If cast one's peek-kind is "Identifier":
                Cast one's advance.
                Cast one's skip-noise.
            Done.
            Cast one's consume on ("With") or pass the failure off.
            Cast one's skip-noise.
            Return cast one's record-shape-body or pass the failure off.
        Done.
        Define base as cast one's type-annotation or pass the failure off.
        Cast one's skip-noise.
        If cast one's peek-kind is "Or" and cast one's kind-after is "Failure":
            Cast one's advance.
            Cast one's skip-noise.
            Cast one's consume on ("Failure") or pass the failure off.
            Cast one's skip-noise.
            Return cast made on ("FailureType", a series with (base)).
        Done.
        If cast one's peek-kind is not "FunctionKw", return base.
        Cast one's advance.
        Cast one's skip-noise.
        Define parameters as cast one's function-param-type-list or pass the failure off.
        Return cast made on ("FunctionType", a series with (parameters, base)).
    Done.

    /// `, given (<type> <name>, …)` — an empty list when there is none.
    Bind node or failure to given-clause unto parser:
        Define parameters as cast listed.
        If cast one's peek-kind is not "Comma" or cast one's past-comma-is on ("Given") is false, return parameters.
        Cast one's advance.
        Cast one's skip-noise.
        Cast one's consume on ("Given") or pass the failure off.
        Cast one's skip-noise.
        Cast one's consume on ("LParen") or pass the failure off.
        Cast one's skip-noise.
        If cast one's peek-kind is not "RParen":
            Define first-parameter as cast one's parameter or pass the failure off.
            Cast parameters's add on (first-parameter).
            Cast one's skip-noise.
            While cast one's peek-kind is "Comma", repeat:
                Cast one's advance.
                Cast one's skip-noise.
                Define next-parameter as cast one's parameter or pass the failure off.
                Cast parameters's add on (next-parameter).
                Cast one's skip-noise.
            Done.
        Done.
        Cast one's consume on ("RParen") or pass the failure off.
        Cast one's skip-noise.
        Return parameters.
    Done.

    /// `[<type> <name>]`, or a function-typed one: `<type> function <name> given (…)`.
    Bind node or failure to parameter unto parser:
        Cast one's skip-noise-before-type.
        If cast one's peek-kind is "Record":
            Cast one's advance.
            Cast one's skip-noise.
            Define record-name as cast one's consume on ("Identifier") or pass the failure off.
            Cast one's skip-noise.
            Cast one's consume on ("With") or pass the failure off.
            Cast one's skip-noise.
            Define shape as cast one's record-shape-body or pass the failure off.
            Define record-pair as cast listed.
            Cast record-pair's add on (shape).
            Cast record-pair's add on (cast quoted on (record-name's lexeme)).
            Return record-pair.
        Done.
        Define returned as cast nothing.
        If cast one's peek-kind is "Void":
            Cast one's advance.
            Cast one's skip-noise.
            If cast one's peek-kind is not "FunctionKw":
                Return a failure (cast one's expecting on (cast one's peek,
                    "function — 'void' can only appear as the return type of a function-typed parameter")).
            Done.
        Done.
        Otherwise:
            The returned becomes cast one's type-annotation or pass the failure off.
            Cast one's skip-noise.
            If cast one's peek-kind is not "FunctionKw":
                Define name-tok as cast one's consume on ("Identifier") or pass the failure off.
                Define pair as cast listed.
                Cast pair's add on (returned).
                Cast pair's add on (cast quoted on (name-tok's lexeme)).
                Return pair.
            Done.
        Done.
        Cast one's advance.
        Cast one's skip-noise.
        Define name-tok as cast one's consume on ("Identifier") or pass the failure off.
        Cast one's skip-noise.
        Define inner as cast one's function-param-type-list or pass the failure off.
        Define pair as cast listed.
        Cast pair's add on (cast made on ("FunctionType", a series with (inner, returned))).
        Cast pair's add on (cast quoted on (name-tok's lexeme)).
        Return pair.
    Done.

    /// A body giving a value back: a comma and the value, or a block.
    Bind fact to is-statement-opener, given (the text kind):
        For each opener-kind in a series with ("State", "Insert", "Increment", "Decrement", "Remove",
                "Replace", "Send", "Close", "Write", "Append", "Open", "Define", "Bind", "If", "While",
                "For", "Try", "Judge", "Stop", "Skip", "GetKw", "SetKw"), repeat:
            If kind is opener-kind, return true.
        Done.
        Return false.
    Done.

    /// ParseValueBodyOrBlock — a comma and the value, or a colon and a block.
    Bind node or failure to value-body unto parser, given (the token opener, the text example, the text construct):
        Cast one's skip-noise.
        If cast one's peek-kind is "Comma":
            Define comma as cast one's advance.
            Cast one's skip-noise.
            Define first-tok as cast one's peek.
            If first-tok's kind is "Return":
                Return a failure (cast one's refused on (first-tok,
                    "an inline body gives its value back on its own, so 'Return' is not written here "
                    joined to "— drop it, as in 'Bind number to double, given (the number n), n * 2.'. "
                    joined to "Use the block form ': ... Done.' if the body needs more than one statement.")).
            Done.
            If cast is-statement-opener on (first-tok's kind):
                Return a failure (cast one's refused on (first-tok,
                    "'{first-tok's lexeme}' opens a statement, but this body has to give a value back, "
                    joined to "so its inline form is an EXPRESSION — the thing to return, with no 'Return'. "
                    joined to "Use the block form ': ... Done.' to run statements.")).
            Done.
            Increment one's nest-depth by 1.
            Define value as cast one's expression or pass the failure off.
            Decrement one's nest-depth by 1.
            Cast one's skip-noise.
            Cast one's consume on ("Dot") or pass the failure off.
            Define body as cast listed.
            Cast body's add on (cast placed on ("ReturnStatement", a series with (value), comma)).
            Return body.
        Done.
        Cast one's consume on ("Colon") or pass the failure off.
        Increment one's nest-depth by 1.
        Define body as cast one's function-body on (opener, example, construct) or pass the failure off.
        Decrement one's nest-depth by 1.
        Return body.
    Done.

    /// ParseVoidBodyOrBlock — a comma and one statement, or a colon and a block.
    Bind node or failure to void-body unto parser, given (the token opener, the text example, the text construct):
        Cast one's skip-noise.
        If cast one's peek-kind is "Comma":
            Cast one's advance.
            Cast one's skip-noise.
            Define first-tok as cast one's peek.
            Increment one's nest-depth by 1.
            Define body as cast listed.
            Try to:
                Define single as cast one's statement.
                Cast body's add on (single).
            Done.
            In case of failure:
                // An EXPRESSION where a statement belongs — "expected Becomes" points at the wrong idea.
                If the message of the failure contains "expected Becomes":
                    Return a failure (cast one's refused on (first-tok,
                        "this body gives nothing back, so its inline form is a STATEMENT, not an "
                        joined to "expression — something like 'State ...' or 'one's field becomes ...'. "
                        joined to "A body that should return a value needs a return type: "
                        joined to "'Bind number to ...' rather than 'Bind void to ...'.")).
                Done.
                Return a failure (the message of the failure).
            Done.
            Decrement one's nest-depth by 1.
            Return body.
        Done.
        Cast one's consume on ("Colon") or pass the failure off.
        Increment one's nest-depth by 1.
        Define body as cast one's function-body on (opener, example, construct) or pass the failure off.
        Decrement one's nest-depth by 1.
        Return body.
    Done.

    /// ParseFunctionBody — statements up to `Done.`, none being fine.
    Bind node or failure to function-body unto parser, given (the token opener, the text example, the text construct):
        Define body as cast listed.
        Define scanning as true.
        While scanning, repeat:
            Cast one's skip-noise.
            If cast one's peek-kind is "Done" or cast one's peek-kind is "Eof", stop.
            Define inner as cast one's statement or pass the failure off.
            Cast body's add on (inner).
        Done.
        If cast one's peek-kind is "Eof":
            Return a failure (cast unclosed on (opener, example, construct)).
        Done.
        Cast one's consume on ("Done") or pass the failure off.
        Cast one's consume on ("Dot") or pass the failure off.
        Return body.
    Done.

    // ── Failures ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    /// PeekHandlerKind — the word after `In case of`, or Eof.
    Bind text to handler-kind unto parser:
        Define spot as cast one's past-noise on (one's at).
        For each expected in a series with ("In", "Case", "Of"), repeat:
            Define here as cast one's token-at on (spot).
            If here's kind is not expected, return "Eof".
            The spot becomes cast one's past-noise on (spot + 1).
        Done.
        Define found as cast one's token-at on (spot).
        Return found's kind.
    Done.

    Bind node or failure to try-statement unto parser:
        Define try-tok as cast one's advance.
        Cast one's skip-noise.
        Cast one's consume on ("To") or pass the failure off.
        Cast one's skip-noise.
        Cast one's consume on ("Colon") or pass the failure off.
        Increment one's nest-depth by 1.
        Define body as cast one's loop-body on (try-tok, "", "", "") or pass the failure off.
        Decrement one's nest-depth by 1.
        Cast one's skip-noise.
        Define on-failure as cast nothing.
        Define on-exception as cast nothing.
        If cast one's handler-kind is "Failure":
            Define handler-tok as cast one's advance.
            Cast one's skip-noise.
            For each word in a series with ("Case", "Of", "Failure"), repeat:
                Cast one's consume on (word) or pass the failure off.
                Cast one's skip-noise.
            Done.
            Cast one's consume on ("Colon") or pass the failure off.
            Increment one's nest-depth by 1.
            The on-failure becomes cast one's loop-body on (handler-tok, "", "In case of failure", "") or pass the failure off.
            Decrement one's nest-depth by 1.
            Cast one's skip-noise.
        Done.
        Define exception-name as "exception".
        If cast one's handler-kind is "Exception":
            Define handler-tok as cast one's advance.
            Cast one's skip-noise.
            For each word in a series with ("Case", "Of", "Exception"), repeat:
                Cast one's consume on (word) or pass the failure off.
                Cast one's skip-noise.
            Done.
            If cast one's peek-kind is "LParen":
                Cast one's advance.
                Cast one's skip-noise.
                If cast one's peek-kind is "Exception":
                    Cast one's advance.
                Done.
                Otherwise:
                    Define named as cast one's consume on ("Identifier") or pass the failure off.
                    The exception-name becomes named's lexeme.
                Done.
                Cast one's skip-noise.
                Cast one's consume on ("RParen") or pass the failure off.
                Cast one's skip-noise.
            Done.
            Cast one's consume on ("Colon") or pass the failure off.
            Increment one's nest-depth by 1.
            The on-exception becomes cast one's loop-body on (handler-tok, "", "In case of exception", "") or pass the failure off.
            Decrement one's nest-depth by 1.
        Done.
        Define attempt as cast placed on ("TryStatement", a series with (body, on-failure, on-exception), try-tok).
        Cast attempt's add on (cast atom on (":ExceptionName")).
        Cast attempt's add on (cast quoted on (exception-name)).
        Return attempt.
    Done.

    // ── Pulls ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    Bind fact to is-book-word unto parser, given (the text word):
        Define here as cast one's peek.
        If here's kind is not "Identifier" or cast spelled on (here, word) is false, return false.
        Define next-tok as cast one's token-at on (one's at + 1).
        Return next-tok's kind is "On".
    Done.

    /// One pulled entry: `<name> [as <local>]`, as a pair.
    Bind node or failure to pull-entry unto parser:
        Define book-tok as cast one's consume on ("Identifier") or pass the failure off.
        Cast one's skip-noise.
        Define local as book-tok's lexeme.
        If cast one's peek-kind is "As":
            Cast one's advance.
            Cast one's skip-noise.
            Define local-tok as cast one's consume on ("Identifier") or pass the failure off.
            The local becomes local-tok's lexeme.
            Cast one's skip-noise.
        Done.
        Define pair as cast listed.
        Cast pair's add on (cast quoted on (book-tok's lexeme)).
        Cast pair's add on (cast quoted on (local)).
        Return pair.
    Done.

    /// Statements up to `Done.` — none is fine, and no nesting is counted.
    Bind node or failure to pull-body unto parser, given (the node books):
        Define introduces as false.
        For each entry in books's children, repeat:
            If ((item 1 of entry's children)'s word in lowercase) is "\"collections\"", the introduces becomes true.
        Done.
        If introduces, increment one's collections-depth by 1.
        Define body as cast listed.
        Define scanning as true.
        While scanning, repeat:
            Cast one's skip-noise.
            If cast one's peek-kind is "Done" or cast one's peek-kind is "Eof", stop.
            Define inner as cast one's statement or pass the failure off.
            Cast body's add on (inner).
        Done.
        Cast one's consume on ("Done") or pass the failure off.
        Cast one's consume on ("Dot") or pass the failure off.
        If introduces, decrement one's collections-depth by 1.
        Return body.
    Done.

    Bind node or failure to pull-statement unto parser:
        Define pull-tok as cast one's advance.
        Cast one's skip-noise.
        Define here as cast one's peek.
        If here's kind is "Identifier" and cast spelled on (here, "rabbit"):
            Cast one's advance.
            Cast one's skip-noise.
            Define name as cast nothing.
            If cast one's peek-kind is "As":
                Cast one's advance.
                Cast one's skip-noise.
                Define name-tok as cast one's consume on ("Identifier") or pass the failure off.
                The name becomes cast quoted on (name-tok's lexeme).
                Cast one's skip-noise.
            Done.
            Cast one's consume on ("Dot") or pass the failure off.
            Increment one's rabbit-depth by 1.
            Define body as cast one's pull-body on (cast listed) or pass the failure off.
            Decrement one's rabbit-depth by 1.
            Return cast placed on ("PullRabbitStatement", a series with (name, body), pull-tok).
        Done.
        Define books as cast listed.
        Define via-book as false.
        If cast one's is-book-word on ("books"):
            Cast one's advance.
            Cast one's skip-noise.
            Cast one's consume on ("On") or pass the failure off.
            Cast one's skip-noise.
            Define first-entry as cast one's pull-entry or pass the failure off.
            Cast books's add on (first-entry).
            Define scanning as true.
            While cast one's peek-kind is "Comma" or cast one's peek-kind is "And", repeat:
                If cast one's peek-kind is "Comma", cast one's advance.
                Cast one's skip-noise.
                If cast one's peek-kind is "And", cast one's advance.
                Cast one's skip-noise.
                If cast one's peek-kind is "Dot", stop.
                Define entry as cast one's pull-entry or pass the failure off.
                Cast books's add on (entry).
            Done.
            The via-book becomes true.
        Done.
        Otherwise if cast one's is-book-word on ("book"):
            Cast one's advance.
            Cast one's skip-noise.
            Cast one's consume on ("On") or pass the failure off.
            Cast one's skip-noise.
            Define entry as cast one's pull-entry or pass the failure off.
            Cast books's add on (entry).
            The via-book becomes true.
        Done.
        Otherwise:
            Define entry as cast one's pull-entry or pass the failure off.
            Cast books's add on (entry).
        Done.
        Cast one's consume on ("Dot") or pass the failure off.
        Define body as cast listed.
        If via-book:
            The body becomes cast one's pull-body on (books) or pass the failure off.
        Done.
        Otherwise:
            The body becomes cast one's pull-body on (cast listed) or pass the failure off.
        Done.
        Return cast made on ("PullStatement", a series with (books, body,
            cast row-of on (pull-tok), cast column-of on (pull-tok), cast flag on (via-book))).
    Done.
Done.
